    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family H). Stand-alone finding F24.5 previously folded onto INV-virik. Full evidence remains on INV-virik's pass-24 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation.\n\n## Symptom\n\nEntrypoint records carry only 4 fields:\n- `confidence`\n- `kind`\n- `label`\n- `symbol_id`\n\nThey lack `evidence_type` / `source` / per-emission provenance fields, unlike Edge records which carry `meta.evidence_type` with a documented vocabulary and other provenance anchors.\n\nConsumers cannot debug entrypoint confidence calibration without provenance: an entrypoint with `confidence=0.6` looks the same regardless of whether it came from `framework_route_detector`, `manifest_target`, or `library_export_heuristic`. The confidence-calibration concern that INV-suvil tracks for Edges has no analog surface for Entrypoints.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEvery Entrypoint record carries an `evidence_type` field drawn from a documented vocabulary, plus a `source` field naming the producer pass. Matches the Edge record's provenance shape.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nTwo parts:\n\n**(a) Schema addition.** Add `Entrypoint.evidence_type: str` and `Entrypoint.source: str` (or relocate under `Entrypoint.meta.evidence_type` if symmetry with Edge is preferred). Producer populates at emission time.\n\n**(b) Writer audit.** Each entrypoint producer is identified (manifest target detector, framework route detector, library export heuristic, ...) and adds the new fields at its emission site. Vocabulary documented in spec.md.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F24.5** — INV-virik discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-24 batch; entrypoint provenance gap).\n\nLab notebook: pass 24 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-virik**.\n- Sibling: **INV-suvil** (Edge confidence calibration; analog for Entrypoint absent — this row fills the gap).\n- Sibling: **WI-entrypoint-record-lacks-id** (Family I — different EP-record gap, also schema-level addition).\n- Family H siblings."  # 73f5
    fields: {}  # 73f5
